		<article class="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-sm border border-gray-100 p-6 sm:p-10">
			<p class="text-brand-red font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-sm mb-3">Procurement Risk Guide</p>
			<h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-black text-gray-900 leading-tight tracking-tight">How to Detect Fake Valves &amp; Counterfeit Fire Equipment Certificates (2026 Buyer Guide)</h1>
			<p class="mt-5 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed text-lg">Buyers of fire valves, hydrants and hoses from China regularly face counterfeit castings, cloned nameplates and forged certificates. A fake unit will not show itself in the photos or the price list — it reveals itself through physical inspection, per-unit test records and documentation you can check independently. This guide gives you the exact signals, a step-by-step detection checklist and a pre-order verification workflow you can attach to any purchase order.</p>

			<div class="bg-blue-50 border border-blue-100 rounded-xl p-5 my-6">
				<p class="text-sm text-gray-700 leading-relaxed"><strong class="text-brand-blue">Why this guide exists:</strong> counterfeit fire equipment is not a hypothetical risk — cloned serials, copied nameplates and forged certification PDFs are the standard playbook of non-compliant suppliers in safety-critical categories. This page turns that risk into a written detection process you can run against any Chinese supplier, including Wanlian Fluid, before you pay.</p>
			</div>

			<!-- Product strip -->
			<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
				{productRows.map(p => (
					<a href={`/products/${p.slug}/`} class="group bg-gray-50 rounded-xl border border-gray-100 overflow-hidden hover:border-brand-red hover:shadow-md transition">
